cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "bsm-public-rf: Reproduction repository for the BSM reduced-form model case study"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hettinger
    given-names: Dylan
    email: dylan.hettinger@nlr.gov
    affiliation: National Renewable Energy Laboratory
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/NatLabRockies/bsm-public-rf"
url: "https://github.com/NatLabRockies/bsm-public-rf"
abstract: >-
  bsm-public-rf is the reproduction repository for a reduced-form modeling case
  study built on the Biomass Scenario Model (BSM), a deterministic system
  dynamics model of U.S. biofuels deployment. It contains the pipeline
  configuration, committed final model artifacts, and driver scripts needed to
  reproduce the published results using the rfm-pipeline framework. The
  reduced-form surrogate maps exogenous simulator inputs to a large set of
  scalar responses through an explicit, portable algebraic model.
keywords:
  - reduced-form modeling
  - surrogate modeling
  - reproducibility
  - sensitivity analysis
  - bioenergy
references:
  - type: software
    title: "rfm-pipeline"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/NatLabRockies/rfm-pipeline"
    authors:
